<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slovenia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Slovenia is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, the Pannonian plain and the Adriatic Sea, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ljubljana">Ljubljana</a>. Its lands, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-styria">Lower Styria</a> and part of the Littoral, were ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> for centuries before joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-slovenes-croats-and-serbs">State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs</a> in 1918 and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>. It declared independence in 1991 and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slovenia.jpg" alt="Slovenia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Marko Pogačnik Vector: Achim1999 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovenia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
